Falsifies `system_tests::user::raw_mode_tests::a_copy_badged_as_stdin_reads_the_typed_line_and_nothing_else`.

Architecture: aarch64

The defect: the terminal serves a `STDIN_BADGE` copy its whole surface, as it served every badged
copy before milestone 709 (a graphical terminal session on the no-keyboard arm holds only the raw
half of the boot discipline) narrowed the raw reader's. `jig`'s standard input could then type a line
the shell runs, print, or switch the terminal's mode.

Expected to fail: the assertion that a stdin holder's `OPERATION_BYTES` is refused ("a stdin
holder's OPERATION_BYTES was served").

The patch lets the stdin badge past `line_editor`'s serve loop whole (`badge ==
proto::STDIN_BADGE ||` ahead of `proto::admits`), because the table itself left the tree with
`terminal_contract`. Replayed red on aarch64 on 2026-11-22 (UTC).

diff --git a/components/src/line_editor.rs b/components/src/line_editor.rs
index 71b08e4ce..23246b281 100644
--- a/components/src/line_editor.rs
+++ b/components/src/line_editor.rs
@@ -159,7 +159,7 @@ fn start(mode: u64, control: u64, start: u64) -> ! {
             reply(slot, proto::BAD_REQUEST, 0);
             continue;
         };
-        if !proto::admits(badge, operation) {
+        if !(badge == proto::STDIN_BADGE || proto::admits(badge, operation)) {
             reply(slot, proto::BAD_REQUEST, 0);
             continue;
         }
